From: 5656565566 <contact@home56.top>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:44:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sched: Charge instance RT to the shared CPU quota

Keep native FIFO/RR priority, runqueue selection and SMP balancing. Charge
managed RT and priority inheritance to the instance's existing CFS CPU
bandwidth hierarchy, shared with ordinary tasks, without fair group
weighting or a second RT runtime pool. Reuse the throttle return-to-user
work and limbo lists; retain the native host RT bandwidth safeguards.

Only the initial user namespace may enable quota mode on an empty finite
unpublished boundary. Descendants inherit that owner and cannot escape it
or remove its finite quota. Instance RT admission uses the sealed owner;
SCHED_DEADLINE admission is not delegated.

Signed-off-by: 5656565566 <contact@home56.top>

